			"notes": "## Location Tooltip 0.7.0\n\nEvery screen has a new look: a navy leather book with paper pages, made to sit right next to Minecraft's own screens.\n\n### Changed\n\n- **The region panel is now a book.** The left page lists your regions with a map icon and how far away each one is. Pick one and the right page shows it on a small map, with its size, centre, owner and protections.\n- **Protections are icons.** Click one to switch between Inherit, Allow and Deny. It turns green or red, and hovering it tells you which flag it is.\n- **Settings fit on one spread.** The left page picks which pills show and the right page sets how they look. Mod Menu opens it straight away, so the extra menu screen is gone.\n- **Buttons, page arrows and tooltips are vanilla.** They look and sound like the rest of the game.\n- **Delete asks twice.** The first press arms it and the second one deletes.\n- **Moving pills shows the screen zones.** While you drag, the zone your pill will stick to lights up.\n- **The compass is called the Admin Compass in game**, matching the wiki. It used to say Master Compass.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- **The region list on 26.x no longer flips between all regions and nearby ones** while you hold the Admin Compass with the book open.\n\n### Notes\n\n- Each Minecraft version is a separate download. Pick the file that matches your game.\n- Villages and temples get their own map icons when the server runs 0.7.0 too. On an older server they show a plain marker.\n- Nothing changes for existing worlds or settings.\n\n---\n*Requires Fabric API. Mod Menu and Waystones are optional.*"
		},
