			"notes": "## Location Tooltip 0.6.0\n\nYou can drag the pills around now, and the settings screen belongs to the mod rather than to another mod.\n\n### Added\n\n- **A HUD editor.** Open the settings and pick Move the pills. The world dims, your pills stay where they are, and you drag them wherever you want. They snap flush to screen edges and to the middle of the screen, with a guide line so you can see it caught. Drop one pill on another and the two join into a neat row, and a row gets a box around it that moves all of them together. Nothing can be dragged off screen.\n\n- **An FPS pill.** Off by default. Turn it on with the others and place it like any of them.\n\n- **The clock has its own place now.** It used to be stuck to the region pill. Put it wherever you like.\n\n### Changed\n\n- **Cloth Config is no longer needed.** The mod draws its own settings screen in the same style as the editor and the region panel. Cloth Config is still listed as an optional dependency so nothing breaks if you have it, but it is not used. This means everyone gets a settings screen, where before you needed Cloth Config or a text editor.\n\n- **Sizing is one slider.** There used to be six settings that all had to move together to make a pill bigger. There is one Size slider now that scales the text and icons as a unit, with padding and height tucked under Fine tuning for the rare occasion you want them. Your existing setup carries over at the same size.\n\n- **The settings screen has sounds** and its sections are properly separated.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- **Corner rounding actually works.** It never has. The corners were being drawn rounded and then filled back in as squares, so any value above 1 gave you a plain rectangle. The slider does something now.\n\n- **Borders draw as a ring around the pill.** They used to be a filled shape behind it, so with a see through background you could see the border through the pill.\n\n- **No more lines across the pills.** With the background below full opacity you could see faint bands where the pill was drawn. Parts of it were being painted twice and the overlap showed. Every pixel is painted once now.\n\n- **The keybind for the region panel has a name.** It has been showing as a raw `key.locationtooltip.open_admin` string in the Controls screen this whole time.\n\n### Notes\n\n- Each Minecraft version is a separate download. Pick the file that matches your game.\n- Your config is upgraded automatically. Pills keep the size and position they had.\n- Nothing changes for existing worlds.\n\n---\n*Requires Fabric API. Mod Menu and Waystones are optional.*"
		},
